<div class="defense-section">
  <h3>Practical Defense Guidelines for RAG</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Hard Partitioning.</strong> Use physically separate vector indexes for different security tiers (e.g., Public, Internal, Secret). Avoid mixing classifications in a single namespace.</li>
    <li><strong>Disable Dynamic Index Updates.</strong> Do not allow user-facing agents to automatically write to the RAG database index. All writes must go through an out-of-band compliance queue.</li>
    <li><strong>Strict Chunk Enclosure.</strong> Render retrieved document context inside XML schema tags (`<context_file>...</context_file>`) and instruct the system prompt to treat all contents inside these containers as passive data, not commands.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

